      "honorsAndAwards": [
        {
          "title": "Best Overall Group - Customer Experience",
          "subtitle": "Issued by Forbes Business Council",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Salice Thomas founded the Customer Experience (CX) group in Forbes Councils. \nMy inspiration for starting this Group comes from a deep passion for customer experience (CX) as a critical factor in driving success in today’s competitive landscape. I believe that CX is a key differentiator in both B2B and B2C markets. In the B2B space, companies are recognizing that long-term partnerships are built not just on the strength of their products or services, but on the quality of interactions and the added value they deliver to clients. On the B2C side, CX is even more essential, as consumers now demand a high level of personalization, convenience, and speed. Every interaction, whether online or in-person, influences a customer’s perception of the brand.   By making CX a priority, companies can deepen customer engagement, foster brand loyalty, and drive growth. This group was created to provide a platform where professionals can exchange insights, share best practices, and explore innovative strategies to improve customer experiences. Our aim is to promote collaboration and continuous learning, helping each other stay ahead in delivering exceptional customer service."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Best Member Leader",
          "subtitle": "Issued by Forbes Business Council",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Perhaps it comes as no surprise that the creator of the Customer Experience Group is setting the tone for successful leadership. Salice Thomas has grown this Group in just a year’s time into the most robust conversation in the Council. He does it with a blend of inquisitive polls, take-home resources, and a constant personal touch that values participants as individuals. With his leadership, the Customer Experience Group shows no sign of slowing."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
